;; M7 HKT-dispatch reference probe #3 -- Applicative `ap` shape. NOT a
;; test-suite fixture. Companion to m7-hkt-probe.tur (Functor `fmap`) and
;; m7-hkt-probe-bind.tur (Monad `bind`).
;;
;; The defining feature of `ap` (vs `fmap`/`bind`) is the FIRST argument
;;   ff : (f (fn [a] b))
;; -- an applied HKT type whose ELEMENT is itself a function type `(fn [a] b)`.
;; This stresses the element-tyvar threading on the arg side (the element of
;; `(f (fn [a] b))` is a fn, not a bare tyvar), where `fmap` had `(f a)` and
;; `bind` had a fn-RETURNING-applied continuation.
;;
;; Run: TUR_M7_HKT=1 ./build/tur run docs/upcoming/v2/m7-hkt-probe-ap.tur; echo $?
;;   -> 42  (TARGET, NOT YET REACHED)
;;
;; STATUS (2026-06-18): BLOCKED on a representational erasure, not on the
;; layer-4 emit machinery. Root cause confirmed by instrumented trace
;; (docs/reported/m7-hkt-ap-fn-element-carrier-erasure.md):
;;
;;   - The CLASS decl side is correct: `(f (fn [a] b))` parses with the nested
;;     fn's `arg0_full`/`result_full_type` preserved as TY_TYVAR `a`/`b` (the
;;     `(fn [int] : int)` you may see in a type_print dump is just lossy
;;     kind-only printing of TY_FN, not an erased decl).
;;   - The VALUE side erases: `(some add1)` elaborates to `(Option ptr<void>)`,
;;     NOT `(Option (fn [int] int))`. Passing a function to a type-variable
;;     parameter (`some [A] [x : A] : (Option A)`) records the arg as the
;;     universal poly carrier `ptr<void>`, dropping the precise fn signature.
;;   - Because `b` (the result element / the wrapped fn's RETURN type) lives
;;     ONLY inside that erased fn, m7_collect_tyvar_bindings cannot recover it:
;;     unifying decl `(f (fn a b))` against actual `(Option ptr<void>)` binds
;;     `f -> Option` but leaves `a`/`b` free. The by-value spec's result `(f b)`
;;     therefore stays the int64 carrier, the spec emits a carrier return, AND
;;     the per-instance dispatch dict is left referencing the (now-dropped)
;;     carrier base method -> a hard cc error (undeclared
;;     `__inst_MyApplicative_ap_Option`).
;;
;; Unblocking ap is the "fat-closure carrier" follow-on flagged in Phase 4.2:
;; thread the precise fn type through polymorphic constructor calls so an
;; Option-of-fn keeps its element signature. That is a broad change, out of
;; scope for a layer-4 emit increment, so ap stays a documented-blocked probe.
;;
;; MITIGATION LANDED (2026-06-18, fix direction 3): a residual free result
;; element tyvar now aborts the by-value HKT monomorphization and falls back to
;; the uniform carrier dispatch (m7_type_has_free_tyvar / m7_byvalue_grounded in
;; src/compiler/elab_typeclasses.c). So under TUR_M7_HKT=1 this probe no longer
;; produces broken C / a cc crash -- it surfaces the SAME clean elaborator type
;; error as the flag-off path:
;;   error [TUR-E0001]: function 'unwrap' arg 1:
;;     expected (type-app Option tyvar 'A'), got (type-app ? ?)
;; The TARGET (exit 42) still awaits fix direction 1.
;;
;; With the flag OFF the probe errors by design (no ascriptions).

(defclass MyApplicative [^f]
  (ap [ff : (f (fn [a] b)) fa : (f a)] : (f b)))

(definstance MyApplicative [Option]
  (ap [ff fa]
    (if (some? ff)
      (if (some? fa)
        (some ((.value ff) (.value fa)))
        (none))
      (none))))

(defn add1 [x : int] : int (+ x 1))

(defn main [] : int
  (let [r (ap (some add1) (some 41))]
    (unwrap r)))   ; TARGET: 42
